Question
Is there a simple way to redact a JSON like this:
{
  "level": "INFO",
  "time": 1762964214879,
  "dd": {
    "trace_id": "xxx6168688b8a3f63ba",
    "span_id": "xxx487694978",
    "service": "blabla",
    "version": "e411a23de49c90b7f480d5aa4dfb1c968b9ca334",
    "env": "prod"
  },
  "headers": {
    "Authorization": "Bearer sensitive-jwt-token-here",
    "token": "internal-secret-shhhh",
    "Content-Type": "application/json"
  },
  "request_path": "/api/v1/login",
  "message": "Test 3: Sensitive headers"
}

into this:
{
  "level": "INFO",
  "time": 1762964214879,
  "dd": {
    "trace_id": "xxx6168688b8a3f63ba",
    "span_id": "xxx487694978",
    "service": "blabla",
    "version": "e411a23de49c90b7f480d5aa4dfb1c968b9ca334",
    "env": "prod"
  },
  "headers": {
    "Authorization": "[REDACTED]",
    "token": "[REDACTED]",
    "Content-Type": "application/json"
  },
  "request_path": "/api/v1/login",
  "message": "Test 3: Sensitive headers"
}

?
I tried already the redact function but it works only on values and not on keys, so if I have a json like:
{ "token": "blabla" }

and I use as a filter r'token' it won't redact anything leaving the value (blabla) untouched
With the attached transforms I achieve it, but I was wondering if it was the most idiomatic way to do it with Vector.
Thank you
Vector Config
transforms:
  parser:
    type: remap
    inputs: [ kubernetes_logs ]
    source: |
      parsed, err = parse_regex(.message, r'(?P<json_str>\{.*\})$')
      if err == null {
        json_map, jerr = parse_json(parsed.json_str)
        if jerr == null && is_object(json_map) {
          del(.message)
          . |= object!(json_map)
        }
      }
